1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,650
Jamsugyo, the bridge you always see in rainy season news, is under water again.

2
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:08,200
But this bridge was made to go under water from the start.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,050
It sits low, right above the Han River, so when the water rises, it goes under.

4
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:17,400
A high bridge costs more and takes longer, so they built it low, short, and fast.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,550
Then they put Banpo Bridge on top as a second floor.

6
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:24,000
So it became a rare two-level bridge.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,600
When water rises, cars are stopped first. When it rises more, people too.

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,450
When the water goes down, they wash off the mud, and cars drive again like nothing happened.
